{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, it would be this:\n\nI'd make sure no one has to live in survival mode.\n\nNo one worrying where their next meal will come from, whether they have a safe place to sleep, or whether anyone would notice if they disappeared.\n\nNot just physical survival, but emotional survival too - that feeling of being alone, unseen, or like you have to hide who you really are to be accepted.\n\nI think so much of the worst in the world - cruelty, greed, division, even apathy - comes from fear and scarcity. When people feel unsafe or unseen, it's so hard to be generous, creative, or kind.\n\nBut when people feel safe and valued? That's when they do amazing things. They help each other, they make art, they take risks, they love more freely.\n\nIf everyone had their basic needs met and knew, deep down, that they mattered to someone, I think almost every other problem would become more solvable. You'd unlock so much human potential that's currently just spent trying to get by.\n\nThat's my one wish.\n\nWhat about you? What's the one thing you would change?",
